 scikit-learn para ajustar los datos"],"metadata":{"collapsed":false,"id":"9WVhQJwXp8or"}},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":null,"outputs":[{"name":"stdout","output_type":"stream","text":["La pendiente del modelo (B) es: [21.56972408], el intersecto (A) es 42.116527260197756\n"]}],"source":["from sklearn.linear_model import LinearRegression\n","\n","# crear el modelo\n","regressor = LinearRegression(fit_intercept = True)\n","# entrenarlo con los datos\n","regressor.fit(X_train, y_train)\n","\n","# el modelo tendrá dos parámetros (A y B fueron llamados en el documento)\n","# se pueden mostrar con la función print\n","print(f\"La pendiente del modelo (B) es: {regressor.coef_}, el intersecto (A) es {regressor.intercept_}\")\n"],"metadata":{"ExecuteTime":{"end_time":"2024-03-19T00:39:45.485663600Z","start_time":"2024-03-19T00:39:45.463472100Z"},"id":"FYeEPcGvp8os","outputId":"32d618c0-6dee-4a7b-e573-9641ba91b130"}},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["### 2.4 Evaluación del modelo"],"metadata":{"collapsed":false,"id":"vpXHNchKp8os"}},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":null,"outputs":[{"data":{"text/plain":"Text(0.5, 1.0, 'Ingresos por ventas de helados respecto a la temperatura')"},"execution_count":16,"metadata":{},"output_type":"execute_result"},{"data":{"text/plain":"<Figure size 640x480 with 1 Axes>","image/png":""},"metadata":{},"output_type":"display_data"}],"source":["y_pred = regressor.predict(X_test)\n","plt.scatter(X_train, y_train, color = 'gray')\n","plt.plot(X_train, regressor.predict(X_train), color = 'red')\n","plt.ylabel('Ingresos [USD]')\n","plt.xlabel('Temperatura [ºC]')\n","plt.title('Ingresos por ventas de helados respecto a la temperatura')"],"metadata":{"ExecuteTime":{"end_time":"2024-03-19T00:39:46.950520500Z","start_time":"2024-03-19T00:39:46.802510500Z"},"id":"rdbTqGVFp8os","outputId":"9ab1ed1e-5079-4139-c4da-3a448de4b7e3"}},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":null,"outputs":[{"data":{"text/plain":"Text(0.5, 1.0, 'Ingresos por ventas de helados respecto a la temperatura (test data)')"},"execution_count":17,"metadata":{},"output_type":"execute_result"},{"data":{"text/plain":"<Figure size 640x480 with 1 Axes>","image/png":""},"metadata":{},"output_type":"display_data"}],"source":["# VISUALIZE TEST SET RESULTS\n","plt.scatter(X_test, y_test, color = 'gray')\n","plt.plot(X_test, regressor.predict(X_test), color = 'red')\n","plt.ylabel('Ingresos [USD]')\n","plt.xlabel('Temperatura [ºC]')\n","plt.title('Ingresos por ventas de helados respecto a la temperatura (test data)')\n"],"metadata":{"ExecuteTime":{"end_time":"2024-03-19T00:39:47.757060700Z","start_time":"2024-03-19T00:39:47.584691800Z"},"id":"VyAVaiJ3p8ot","outputId":"ec8d1967-0cae-4cba-99a1-401c64e344e8"}},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["\n","### Error medio cuadrático\n","Es una de las medidas más empleadas como función de pérdida en los algoritmos de regresión. Mide la distancia cuadrática entre una predicción del modelo respecto al dato correspondiente en el conjunto de datos para todos los puntos que tenga el conjunto de datos. Luego calcula el promedio de esas distancias.\n","\n"],"metadata":{"collapsed":false,"id":"INkajcx9p8ot"}},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":null,"outputs":[{"name":"stdout","output_type":"stream","text":["Mean Squared Error: 635.1413843141902\n","Root Mean Squared Error: 25.20201151325406\n"]}],"source":["# evaluando el comportamiento del modelo\n","from sklearn.metrics import mean_squared_error\n","print(\"Mean Squared Error:\",mean_squared_error(y_test, y_pred))\n","print(\"Root Mean Squared Error:\",np.sqrt(mean_squared_error(y_test, y_pred)))\n","\n"],"metadata":{"ExecuteTime":{"end_time":"2024-03-19T00:39:48.724128100Z","start_time":"2024-03-19T00:39:48.720460600Z"},"id":"TZVo2lhMp8ot","outputId":"ea1f9447-b0d4-4d5a-94ef-72d6122aed65"}},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["# Error medio absoluto\n","Es la diferencia entre los valores estimados y los reales. Se calcula el promedio de todas las diferencias para encontrar el valor del error"],"metadata":{"collapsed":false,"id":"IIleZEuap8ot"}},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["\n","## Tarea:\n","\n","Error cuadratico medio == mse (mean squared error)\n","\n","```\n","# Error medio absoluto == mae (mean_absolute_error)\n","\n","absolute = abs() en Python\n","\n","| x | = +x, si x>=0\n","| x | = -x, si x<=0\n","\n","Ejemplo:\n","| (5) | = +(5) = +5 = 5\n","| (-5) | = -(-5) = +5 = 5\n","\n","15 = | 40 - 25 | = | 15 | = 15\n","15 = | 25 - 40 | = | -15 | = -(-15)= 15\n","\n","def get_mean_absolute_error(y_real, y_pred):\n","  mae = | (y_real) - (y_pred) |\n","  # mae = | (y_pred) - (y_real) |\n","  return mae\n","```\n","\n"],"metadata":{"id":"RgULs_nQrur7"}},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":null,"outputs":[{"name":"stdout","output_type":"stream","text":["Mean Absolute Error: 19.21536367504677\n"]}],"source":["from sklearn.metrics import mean_absolute_error\n","print(\"Mean Absolute Error:\",mean_absolute_error(y_test, y_pred))"],"metadata":{"ExecuteTime":{"end_time":"2024-03-19T00:39:49.832658400Z","start_time":"2024-03-19T00:39:49.829431200Z"},"id":"g76AY2hVp8ou","outputId":"f9492fc6-d9f9-4018-8636-b4d4b5db9ab0"}},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["### R cuadrado\n","Es una medida estadística que indica que tan cerca estan los datos de ajustarse a una línea recta. Se conoce también como el coeficiente de determinación."],"metadata":{"collapsed":false,"id":"IhYgatZ9p8ou"}},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":null,"outputs":[{"name":"stdout","output_type":"stream","text":["R^2: 0.978151689591555\n"]}],"source":["from sklearn.metrics import r2_score\n","print(\"R^2:\",r2_score(y_test, y_pred))"],"metadata":{"ExecuteTime":{"end_time":"2024-03-19T00:39:52.583273100Z","start_time":"2024-03-19T00:39:52.580680300Z"},"id":"f9XACKg6p8ou","outputId":"d048cd03-eba8-4634-c5d4-ee46a09647d4"}},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["# Sección 3: regresión polinómica\n","\n","Se crearán datos sintéticos para realizar la regrresión a un polinomio.\n"],"metadata":{"collapsed":false,"id":"p2G3l7W_p8ou"}},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":null,"outputs":[{"data":{"text/plain":"Text(0.5, 1.0, 'Dataset generado')"},"execution_count":21,"metadata":{},"output_type":"execute_result"},{"data":{"text/plain":"<Figure size 640x480 with 1 Axes>","image/png":""},"metadata":{},"output_type":"display_data"}],"source":["x_data = np.linspace(0,8,500) # datos en X\n","y_data = 0.125*x_data**3 - x_data**2 + 0.125*x_data  # polinomio con los datos (cúbico)\n","y_data2 = np.random.normal(0,0.50,500) + y_data\n","plt.scatter(x_data, y_data2, c='r', )\n","plt.plot(x_data, y_data) # graficar los datos\n","plt.title(\"Dataset generado\")"],"metadata":{"ExecuteTime":{"end_time":"2024-03-19T00:39:54.199885800Z","start_time":"2024-03-19T00:39:54.033732600Z"},"id":"IMw7o8HYp8ou","outputId":"661159e0-2aa6-499e-8bc8-4e060d08f8c2"}},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["Para la regresión con un polinomio, se necesita preprocesar los datos `x_data` para que modelen un polinomio del grado indicado. Esto es, crear la matriz A para resolver el problema de la forma $Ax = b$, las dimensiones de la matriz A son de $m\\times m$ siendo m el grado del polinomio\n","\n","**Ejercicio**: Variar el grado del polinomio. Los datos corresponden a un polinomio de tercer grado, Se puede apreciar que con grados inferiores los datos van a tener un mal ajuste y con grados superiores puede existir sobre entrenamiento, por ejemplo de grado 20 se empiezan a notar problemas de ajuste"],"metadata":{"collapsed":false,"id":"zoFO-phLp8ov"}},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":null,"outputs":[{"data":{"text/plain":"[<matplotlib.lines.Line2D at 0x7fa135556750>]"},"execution_count":22,"metadata":{},"output_type":"execute_result"},{"data":{"text/plain":"<Figure size 640x480 with 1 Axes>","image/png":""},"metadata":{},"output_type":"display_data"}],"source":["# creando un objeto para la regresión polinómica\n","\n","from sklearn.preprocessing import PolynomialFeat